# design-exploration: what stays local.
# Everything listed here is kept on disk as evidence; it is only kept out of
# Git to keep the repository lean or because it may not be redistributed.
# Rules are deliberately narrow (explicit folders and file types) so no
# documentation, prototype source or generator can be hidden by accident.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Third-party visual references (Pinterest): study material only, not
# licensed for redistribution (see references/README.md). The README is tracked.
/references/*.jpg
/concepts/primer-visual-lab/exploration-b/racing-editorial-reference.png

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Stitch concept exports (generated HTML and screenshots). The concept
# specifications and metadata (*.md) are tracked.
/concepts/**/*.html
/concepts/**/*.png

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated validation output. Every prototype validation pass writes its
# screenshots, measurement JSON, text reports and a copy of its capture
# scripts into a timestamped folder named
# validation-YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS[-label]/. Those folders are run output, not
# source: they are excluded from the published repository (2026-11 history
# consolidation) and the historical runs are retained in the original-history
# backup. The pattern matches only directories under prototypes/ whose name
# starts with that exact timestamp, so prototype pages, generators
# (build.py, checks-*.mjs), tools and documents can never match it.
/prototypes/**/validation-[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]*/
